.TH LIBDATAMOVEMENT 3 "2025-07-07" "HPE" "Data Movement Offload Client Library"
.SH NAME
libdatamovement \- C library for offloaded data copy operations via a network service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <copy-offload.h>
.br
.B #include <copy-offload-status.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B libdatamovement
library provides an API for submitting, monitoring, and managing data copy operations offloaded to a remote server. It is designed to interact with a copy-offload service, supporting secure (TLS) communication, authentication via workflow tokens, and integration with containerized environments.

The library uses libcurl for HTTP(S) communication and supports both synchronous and asynchronous workflows for data movement. Status and progress of copy jobs can be queried and interpreted using the provided status response API.
.SH DATA TYPES
.TP
.B COPY_OFFLOAD
A handle to a copy-offload client session. All operations require a pointer to an initialized
.BR COPY_OFFLOAD
structure.
.TP
.B copy_offload_status_response_t
A structure representing the parsed status of a data movement request, as returned by
.BR copy_offload_status (3).
It contains state, status, messages, timing, and command progress information.
.TP
.B _copy_offload_command_status_s
Describes the current state of the data movement command, including progress, elapsed time, last message, and the command invoked.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B DW_WORKFLOW_TOKEN
The workflow token for authentication.
.TP
.B NNF_CONTAINER_LAUNCHER
Name of the container running the MPI launcher (used for server address resolution).
.TP
.B NNF_CONTAINER_PORTS
Ports the container is listening on; the library uses the first port.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/local-rabbit.conf
Fallback file for determining the associated server host if
.B NNF_CONTAINER_LAUNCHER
is unset.
.TP
.B /etc/nnf-dm-usercontainer/cert.pem
Default certificate file for TLS connections.
.SH API VERSION
Library and server communicate using the API version "1.0".
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Initialization and Cleanup
.TP
.BI "COPY_OFFLOAD *copy_offload_init(void);"
Create and initialize a handle for a new session.
.TP
.BI "void copy_offload_cleanup(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload);"
Release all resources associated with the handle.
.SS Configuration
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_configure(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload);"
Configure the handle for server communication with TLS enabled.
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure (error in
.IR offload->err_message ).
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_configure_without_tls(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload);"
Configure the handle for server communication without TLS.
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_override_cert(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload, char *cert_path);"
Override the default TLS certificate path.
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_override_token(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload, char *token_path);"
Override the default workflow token. Set
.I token_path
to NULL to disable token use.
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_override_hostname(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload, char *hostname);"
Override the default hostname (default is the system hostname).
.SS Data Movement Operations
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_copy(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload, const char *profile_name, int slots, int max_slots, int dry_run, char *source_path, char *dest_path, char **output);"
Submit a new copy-offload request.
.RS
.TP
.I profile_name
Copy profile to use.
.TP
.I slots, max_slots
Resource allocation.
.TP
.I dry_run
If nonzero, simulate only.
.TP
.I source_path, dest_path
Source and destination paths.
.TP
.I output
On success, set to newly created job name (caller must free).
.RE
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_list(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload, char **output);"
List active copy-offload jobs.
.I output
is a comma-separated list of job names (caller must free).
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_status(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload, char *job_name, int max_wait_secs, copy_offload_status_response_t **status_response);"
Query the status of a copy-offload job.
.RS
.TP
.I job_name
Job identifier.
.TP
.I max_wait_secs
Wait time (0 = immediate, -1 = indefinite).
.TP
.I status_response
Response object (caller must call
.BR copy_offload_status_cleanup ).
.RE
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.BI "void copy_offload_status_cleanup(copy_offload_status_response_t *status_response);"
Free resources associated with a status response. After this call, the
.I status_response
pointer and its fields must not be accessed.
.TP
.BI "void copy_offload_status_pretty_print(FILE *out, copy_offload_status_response_t *status_response);"
Pretty-print the status response to the given file stream. Output includes state, status, message, command, progress, elapsed time, last message, last message time, start time, and end time.
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_cancel(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload, char *job_name, char **output);"
Cancel a specific copy-offload job.
.I output
is the server response, if any (caller must free).
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_shutdown(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload);"
Shutdown the server and exit cleanly.
.SS Development and Debugging
.TP
.BI "void copy_offload_verbose(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload);"
Enable verbose output from libcurl for debugging.
.TP
.BI "int copy_offload_hello(COPY_OFFLOAD *offload, char **output);"
Send a hello message to the server.
.I output
is the server response (caller must free).
Returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.SS Status Response Parsing
.TP
.BI "copy_offload_status_response_t *_copy_offload_status_parse(char *json_text);"
Parse a JSON status response into a
.B copy_offload_status_response_t
structure. Used internally by the library.
.SH STATUS RESPONSE STRUCTURE
The
.B copy_offload_status_response_t
structure describes the current state and progress of a data movement request. Its fields include:
.TP
.B state
Current state of the request (e.g., "Running", "Completed", "Failed").
.TP
.B status
Current status string from the server.
.TP
.B message
Any extra information supplied with the state/status.
.TP
.B command_status
A
.B _copy_offload_command_status_s
structure describing the running command:
.RS
.TP
.B command
Command used to perform data movement.
.TP
.B progress
Progress percentage (0-100) based on the output of
.BR dcp .
.TP
.B elapsed_time
Duration the operation has been running (e.g., "1m30s").
.TP
.B last_message
Most recent output line from the data movement command.
.TP
.B last_message_time
Time of the last message.
.RE
.TP
.B start_time
Start time (local) of the operation.
.TP
.B end_time
End time (local) of the operation.
.SH ERROR HANDLING
Most functions return 0 on success and 1 on failure.
On failure, a human-readable error message is placed in
.IR offload->err_message .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
COPY_OFFLOAD *off = copy_offload_init();
if (copy_offload_configure(off) != 0) {
    fprintf(stderr, "Error: %s\\n", off->err_message);
    exit(1);
}
char *job_name = NULL;
if (copy_offload_copy(off, "default", 1, 1, 0, "/src", "/dst", &job_name) == 0) {
    printf("Submitted job: %s\\n", job_name);
    free(job_name);
}
copy_offload_status_response_t *status = NULL;
if (copy_offload_status(off, job_name, 0, &status) == 0) {
    copy_offload_status_pretty_print(stdout, status);
    copy_offload_status_cleanup(status);
}
copy_offload_cleanup(off);
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
libcurl(3),
json-c(3),
copy-offload-status.h
